NAME

view - Read a text file in the fullscreen pager

SYNOPSIS

    view FILE
    view --help

DESCRIPTION

`view` opens one file in a read-only fullscreen pager. Text wraps by visual
row, and search highlights matching text. The viewer does not modify the file.

OPTIONS

    -h, --help — Show concise invocation help and exit.

KEYBINDINGS

    j — Scroll down one visual row.
    Down — Scroll down one visual row.
    k — Scroll up one visual row.
    Up — Scroll up one visual row.
    Page Down — Scroll down one viewport.
    Space — Scroll down one viewport.
    Page Up — Scroll up one viewport.
    g — Move to the beginning of the document.
    Home — Move to the beginning of the document.
    G — Move to the end of the document.
    End — Move to the end of the document.
    ? — Open incremental search.
    n — Move to the next search match without wrapping.
    b — Move to the previous search match without wrapping.
    Escape — Exit search input or search mode; otherwise close the viewer.
    q — Close the viewer.

During search input, Enter accepts the query and selects the nearest match.
Backspace and Delete edit the query. Escape cancels an unfinished query or
leaves search mode at the current reading position. Search does not wrap at
the document boundaries.

EXAMPLES

    view notes.txt

NOTES

The pager uses Mangrove's scalar-based text-cell layout. It wraps at supported
cell boundaries and does not provide grapheme-aware editing, wide-character
layout, bidirectional ordering, or complex-script shaping. A file that cannot
be read is reported before the pager takes over the console.

